    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0757" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg637"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1210.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 2435 of September 10
                        last,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d629-f1"/> stating that the Mexican judicial
                    authorities were conducting the investigation of the murder of J. B. Maxwell, J.
                    C. Maxwell, and Enoch Woodworth, I have to say that the Department would be
                    pleased to receive a report from you as to the present status of the case.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
